This tower houses ladies of the court, unmarried girls and spinster women, mainly.	這座塔主要住著宮廷仕女，多是未婚少女與未嫁的婦人。
You cannot actually see in from here, but I believe it is the ladies' sewing room inside.  Hardly of interest to you.	你在此處看不進去，但我想裡頭是女眷的針線房。你對此應無興趣。
The fountain has run dry, like most of Camelot's water.	這座噴泉已然乾涸，如同肯萊特大半的水源。
There is none.  The Queen's fountain has dried up, like so many of Camelot's lakes and rivers.  It is one more reminder of the curse which you alone can undo by finding the Grail.	沒有了。王后的噴泉已經乾涸，如同肯萊特眾多的湖泊與河流一般。這又提醒你：唯有尋得聖杯，才能解除這詛咒。
It is a plain stone bench.	這是一張樸素的石凳。
They are dying from the curse upon Camelot.	它們正因肯萊特所受的詛咒而枯死。
You often hunt those hills, even as far as the distant Mendip Hills. But this is no time to be daydreaming.	你常在那片丘陵狩獵，甚至遠至門迪普丘陵。但此刻不是耽於幻想的時候。
I have all the wealth I need and desire no more earthly goods, only the salvation of our land.	我所需的財富已然足夠，不再渴求塵世的財物，只盼我們的國土得到拯救。
You have better things to do than peek into the ladies' sewing room.	你有更要緊的事得做，何必窺探女眷的針線房。
This is not the time for scrambling about like a boy.	此刻不是像個孩子般東奔西跑的時候。
Wanton violence taints the soul.	恣意的暴力會玷污靈魂。
Though you may desire to sit in the sun, your mission is too urgent to wait.	你或許渴望坐下曬曬陽光，但你的使命緊迫，容不得等待。
None of these leaves has any particular value.	這些葉子並無特別的價值。
The only rose has already been picked.	唯一的那朵玫瑰已經摘下了。
You don't need to.	你不需要這麼做。
You would be a poor husband indeed to be so careless.	若你如此粗心大意，實在稱不上是個好丈夫。
She was being poetic, Arthur. She meant only to carry it with you.	她只是說得詩意些罷了，亞瑟。她的意思不過是要你隨身帶著它。
There is nothing quite as exciting as a man with a long sword.	沒有什麼比佩著長劍的男子更令人心動的了。
Fond as I am of your sword, Arthur, I would rather that you save it for a better use.	亞瑟，我雖鍾愛你的劍，但寧可你將它留待更好的用處。
Your sword is unequalled in all of Christendom.  But for my peace of mind, I prefer to see it sheathed.	你的劍在整個基督教世界裡無人能及。但為了我心安，我還是希望見它入鞘。
Arthur, the gods are jealous of their gold. It would be the greatest sacrilege, one which cannot be undone. Think again before you try this.	亞瑟，諸神看重他們的金子。此舉將是莫大的褻瀆，一旦犯下便無可挽回。動手之前，再三思量。
Since you are determined to commit this sacrilege, I will say nothing more. Your doom is your own.	既然你執意要犯下這等褻瀆，我便不再多言。你的劫數，自行承擔。
Fool.	愚蠢。
Arthur, it is not wise to insult a god. Think before you do this.	亞瑟，觸怒神明並非明智之舉。動手之前，先想清楚。
Alas, I fear you bring much evil upon yourself by such an unwise act.	唉，恐怕你這般輕率之舉，會為自己招來重重災禍。
Unwise, Arthur, unwise.	不智啊，亞瑟，太不智了。
The sacred fire of Mithras is lit. The blessing has been given.	米夏拉的聖火已然點燃，恩賜已然降下。
Only the blessing of Mithras can light this candle.	唯有米夏拉的恩賜，才能點燃這支蠟燭。
The sacred fire of Christ is lit. The blessing has been given.	基督的聖火已然點燃，恩賜已然降下。
Only the blessing of Christ can light this candle.	唯有基督的恩賜，才能點燃這支蠟燭。
The ceiling arches over your head like the great vaults of heaven.	天花板在你頭頂拱起，宛如浩瀚的天穹。
The floor is made of inlaid stones.	地板由鑲嵌的石塊鋪成。
There is nothing but a dark space.	那裡除了一片黑暗，什麼也沒有。
Those are pads to kneel upon.	那些是供人跪拜的墊子。
Look again.  Methinks you are confused.	再看仔細些，我看你是糊塗了。
There is only one thing more deadly than offending a god.	世上只有一件事，比觸怒一位神明更為致命。
Offending two gods.	那便是同時觸怒兩位神明。
The cross is an ancient symbol that has been adopted by the followers of the Christ god.	十字是個古老的符號，後為基督信徒所採用。
The symbol of Mithras has emblazoned many a warrior's shield, for he has been primarily a soldier's god.	米夏拉的標識曾裝點過無數戰士的盾牌，因為他向來是軍人的守護神。
Those are symbols of Isis and Vesta. What they are doing in this chapel, I do not know.	那些是艾西斯與維斯塔的標識。它們為何會出現在這座神殿裡，我也不得而知。
This is a relatively new religion, but it has grown enormously in power over the last few centuries. Most of your people now worship the Christ god.	這是一個相對年輕的信仰，但在過去幾個世紀裡勢力大增。如今你的子民多半信奉基督。
Mithras the warrior god has been worshipped for many, many centuries and was the favorite of Roman soldiers.	戰神米夏拉受人供奉已有數百年之久，向來深受羅馬士兵愛戴。
On the right is the altar of Christ.  On the left is the altar of Mithras.	右側是基督的祭壇，左側是米夏拉的祭壇。
The double altar in the Chapel of the Two Gods reflects the power struggle between an old and new religion.	雙神神殿裡的這座雙祭壇，映照出新舊信仰之間的權力角力。
Most of this room is made of stone: the altars, the floor, the pillars.	這房間大半以石造成：祭壇、地板、廊柱皆然。
The walls are lined with decorative columns.	牆邊立著一排裝飾用的廊柱。
They hold up the ceiling.	它們撐起了天花板。
The intertwining lines upon the double altar is Celtic knotwork.	雙祭壇上交纏的線條，是凱爾特結紋。
The highly decorative pillar is one of the main supports for the ceiling.	這根裝飾繁複的廊柱，是支撐天花板的主要柱子之一。
The vision is sent to remind you that you must be morally pure to possess it.  Every deed and decision in your mission will be weighed in judgement.	這異象是要提醒你：唯有心靈純淨之人才配擁有它。你此行的一言一行、每個抉擇，都將受到審判衡量。
Mithras shows you perils that have befallen or will befall your three knights.  He reminds you that, as king, you are responsible for their lives.	米夏拉向你展示你三位騎士已經或即將遭遇的險境，提醒你身為君王，須對他們的性命負責。
I hope you are not seeing something that I do not see. It would not bode well for your mission.	我盼你所見並非我未曾見過之物，否則對你的使命絕非吉兆。
They are not bowls.  They are altar candles.	那些不是碗，是祭壇上的蠟燭。
Upon the right is the cross, symbol of the Christ god who was crucified upon one.	右邊是十字，基督便是被釘死在十字架上，因而成了祂的標識。
Upon the left is the symbol of Mithras, formerly carried upon banners into battle.	左邊是米夏拉的標識，昔日曾被繡上軍旗、隨軍出征。
Only the blessing of Mithras can light the candle on the left.	唯有米夏拉的恩賜，才能點燃左側的蠟燭。
Only the blessing of Christ can light the candle on the right.	唯有基督的恩賜，才能點燃右側的蠟燭。
I am sure you will think of something to offer the gods.	我相信你會想出該獻給諸神什麼供品。
The labarum is the symbol of Mithras.	拉巴倫是米夏拉的標識。
The skulls are reminders of the death that awaits us all.	這些骷髏頭提醒著世人，死亡終將降臨眾生。
And may the god of your choice protect you.	願你所選的神明護佑於你。
That is beyond your powers. Or mine.	那超出了你的能力範圍，也超出了我的。
That can be arranged.	這可以安排。
Not in this place. You need all the help you can get.	此處不可。你需要一切能得到的助力。
The gods are always fond of offerings.  Depending, of course, upon what it is you intend to offer.	諸神向來喜愛供品，當然，這得看你打算獻上什麼。
That is not the sort of offering the gods desire.	那並非諸神所欲的供品。
The candle is not lit.	這支蠟燭並未點燃。
I do not understand what you hope to gain by having burnt fingers.	我不明白你燙傷手指究竟想換得什麼。
It is said that the gods prefer prayers offered upon bended knee.	據說諸神偏愛跪地獻上的禱告。
Perhaps the gods need more tangible proof of your devotion before they will grant a blessing.	或許諸神在賜下恩典之前，需要更實質的證明，證明你的虔誠。
The lighting of the sacred fire is the god's way of telling you that your prayers are heard.	聖火燃起，便是神明告訴你祂已聽見你禱告的方式。
The gods prefer to hear prayers from bended knee.	諸神偏愛聽見跪地獻上的禱告。
Arthur, pay attention.  You are already on your knees.	亞瑟，留意些。你已經跪著了。
It does not require a wizard to see that you ARE standing.	不必是巫師也看得出，你現在正站著。
Humbling yourself is the first step in dealing with any god.	謙卑自抑，是與任何神明打交道的第一步。
Your prayers have been heard and the blessing given.	你的禱告已蒙垂聽，恩賜已然降下。
You have incurred Mithras' wrath.  Nothing can help you now.	你已招來米夏拉的怒火，如今再無挽回餘地。
I suspect that an earthly gift may help your prayers to reach the heavens.	我猜想，一份塵世的供品或許有助於你的禱告上達天聽。
You have incurred Christ's wrath.  Nothing can help you now.	你已招來基督的怒火，如今再無挽回餘地。
You have no money.	你身無分文。
Before a god will accept money, he must be shown the proper reverence.	神明接受供奉之前，須先受到應有的敬意。
The vision was a gift, not a purchase. It will not appear again.	那異象是一份恩賜，並非可以買來的東西，它不會再度出現。
You would not listen to warnings.  Now you are under Mithras' curse and nothing can undo it.	你不聽勸誡，如今已受米夏拉的詛咒，再無法解除。
You have already been blessed.	你已蒙受恩賜。
The dull clunk of a copper coin does not seem to excite much interest from the gods of this chapel.	一枚銅幣落地的悶響，似乎難以引起這神殿諸神的興趣。
The vision was a gift, not a purchase.  It will not appear again.	那異象是一份恩賜，並非可以買來的東西，它不會再度出現。
You would not listen to warnings.  Now you are under Christ's curse and nothing can undo it.	你不聽勸誡，如今已受基督的詛咒，再無法解除。
That would require preparations and priests and too much time. The blessing of the god is enough to ask for.	那需要諸多準備、祭司主持，還要耗費太多時間。只求神明的恩賜便已足夠。
And bring down the curse of the god? Do not even think it!	還要招來神明的詛咒？想都別想！
Your doom is now sealed.	你的劫數已然註定。
There are no gold coins upon the altar.	祭壇上沒有金幣。
There are no silver coins upon the altar.	祭壇上沒有銀幣。
The gods may not notice the loss of a bit of copper.	少了一點銅幣，諸神或許不會察覺。
There are no copper coins upon the altar.	祭壇上沒有銅幣。
If you wish to get more money, you must go to the Treasury. In this place, you should think only in terms of giving.	你若想取得更多錢財，須前往寶庫。在此處，你該想的只有給予。
Which coin do you want?	你要哪一種錢幣？
It would make a lovely offering, but is not quite what the gods want.	這雖是件討喜的供品，卻不是諸神真正想要的。
You're not close enough to a flame and you do not want to be.  Trust me.	你離火焰還不夠近，而你也不會想要靠得更近。相信我。
The fire is not lit on this candle, Arthur	這支蠟燭上並未點著火，亞瑟
Burn a gift of love from Gwenhyver?  I would seriously reconsider.	燒掉昆海兒所贈的愛的信物？我勸你三思。
Nothing is left but ashes.  I sense you have angered the gods and no good will come of this.	只剩下一堆灰燼。我感覺得到，你已觸怒了諸神，此事絕無好結果。
You have not yet been given the blessing of the flame.	你尚未獲得聖火的恩賜。
Are you mad?  It is a sign that Christ has heard your prayers and given his blessing.	你瘋了嗎？那是基督已聽見你禱告、賜下恩典的徵兆。
Mithras has ways of punishing fools who tamper with his holy fire.	米夏拉自有懲罰之道，對付膽敢褻瀆他聖火的愚人。
There. You have nothing better to show for it than burnt fingers.	瞧，除了燙傷的手指，你什麼也沒換到。
That belongs here and is of no use to you.	那東西屬於此處，對你毫無用處。
Those are not bowls.  Those are altar candles and must be left on the altars.	那些不是碗，是祭壇上的蠟燭，必須留在祭壇上。
Only the blessing of a god can do that.	唯有神明的恩賜，才能做到這一點。
The Christ god does not approve of such things.	基督不贊同這樣的事。
Once, in very ancient times, the sacrifice of a white bull would have been proper.  But there is no time for that now.	遠古之時，獻上一頭白牛原本才是合宜的祭品。但如今，已沒有時間這麼做了。
You cannot draw your sword from your knees.	你跪著時無法拔劍。
You annoy the gods by brandishing a weapon in this sacred place.	在這神聖之地揮舞兵刃，會惹惱諸神。
Your knees must be getting sore.  Perhaps you should consider doing something.	你的膝蓋想必已經跪痠了。或許你該考慮做點什麼。
The flame is lit and the blessing given, but wait....	聖火已點燃，恩賜已降下，但且慢……
Mithras sends you visions of your missing knights. And listen! Their voices call out to you in distress!	米夏拉向你展示你失蹤騎士們的異象。且聽！他們的聲音正痛苦地向你呼喚！
Save me, most valiant king! I am injured unto the death by a black fiend. The green leaves will cover my bones unless you are quick.	救救我，至勇的王啊！我為一個黑暗惡魔所傷，命在旦夕。你若不快，青葉終將覆蓋我的白骨。
Arthur, I cannot move. I cannot escape. And I am so cold, so terribly cold. Ah, how can she be so heartless?!	亞瑟，我動彈不得，無法逃脫。我好冷，冷得徹骨。啊，她怎能如此狠心？！
I am lost in the darkness, hidden from light and life, with only the rats to lust for my flesh and blood. I will die here unless you help me, my king.	我迷失在黑暗之中，不見天光，不見生機，唯有鼠群覬覦著我的血肉。吾王，你若不來救我，我將死在此處。
The flame is lit. You have been blessed, and now something shimmers in the air....	聖火已點燃，你已蒙受恩賜，此刻空氣中似有什麼正閃爍著微光……
A vision of the Grail appears to you. Christ sends it to remind you that only a man of purity may attain this sacred cup.	聖杯的異象在你眼前浮現。基督藉此提醒你：唯有心靈純淨之人，方能得到這只聖爵。
Remember, the fate of Camelot rests not only upon your finding the Grail, but your worthiness to possess it.	切記，肯萊特的命運不僅繫於你能否尋得聖杯，更繫於你是否配得擁有它。
That is quite impossible.	那絕無可能。
The gods do not provide visions upon demand.  Accept what you have been given or you will anger them.	諸神不會應人所求便賜下異象。接受你已得到的，否則將觸怒他們。
The gods give visions to those who please them.	諸神只將異象賜給令祂們喜悅的人。
What you saw and heard may have happened or is yet to happen. To learn more, you must find the knights themselves.	你所見所聞，或許已經發生，或許尚未發生。若想知道更多，你必須親自找到那幾位騎士。
The sacred flame is lit. You and your mission have been blessed.	聖火已然點燃。你與你的使命，皆已蒙受恩賜。
The guards stand at attention in your presence.	衛兵們在你面前肅立戒備。
The guard has the air of a man who wants to speak, but is afraid to speak without permission.	這名衛兵神情像是有話想說，卻又不敢未經允許便開口。
You can't take your horse in the castle.	你不能把坐騎帶進城堡裡。
The stables are nearby, but your servants tend to all your needs there. You have other, more important concerns.	馬廄就在附近，但那裡有僕從為你打理一切所需。你還有其他更要緊的事得操心。
